<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yasser Arafat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1929">1929</a>–<a href="/years/2004">2004</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Abu Ammar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yasser Arafat was the Palestinian nationalist leader who chaired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine-liberation-organization">Palestine Liberation Organization</a> from 1969 until his death and became the face of the Palestinian cause. A founder of Fatah in 1959, he pursued armed struggle and later negotiation, addressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> in 1974, signed the Oslo Accords with Israel in 1993, shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1994 and led the new Palestinian Authority from Ramallah. He died near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 2004 with Palestinian statehood unresolved.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yasser-arafat.jpg" alt="Yasser Arafat" width="330" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gideon Markowiz · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leader_of_the_PLO,_Yasser_Arafat,_1996_Dan_Hadani_Archive.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Israel and the PLO signed the Declaration of Principles at the White House, with a historic handshake between Yitzhak Rabin and <b>Yasser Arafat</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-13">13 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The Palestine Liberation Organization, founded in 1964 and led from 1969 by <b>Yasser Arafat</b>, came to stand for Palestinian nationhood after the Nakba of 1948 had scattered much of the Arab population of Mandatory Palestine.</blockquote><a href="/state/state-of-palestine">State of Palestine</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Cairo, in what is now <a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a>. Died in Hôpital d'instruction des armées Percy, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=30.04,31.24&amp;year=1977" aria-label="Cairo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5361 1067 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Yasser Arafat"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5811 1337h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=30.04,31.24&amp;year=1977">What was here in 1977? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
